.TH NAVI-INDEXER 1 "October 2026" "transmission-navi 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
navi-indexer \- generate a static media catalog from Transmission RPC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B navi-indexer
.RB [ \-config " file" ]
.RB [ \-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B navi-indexer
queries a Transmission RPC endpoint, parses torrent and file names, maps NAS
filesystem paths to SMB URLs, optionally enriches movies through TMDB, and
atomically writes a JSON catalog for the Transmission Navi web interface.
.PP
The program performs one refresh and exits. The packaged systemd timer invokes
it every 15 minutes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " file"
Read JSON configuration from
.IR file .
Environment variables override corresponding JSON values.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the program version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/transmission-navi/config.json
Packaged configuration. It can contain credentials and must remain protected.
.TP
.I /var/lib/transmission-navi/catalog.json
Default generated catalog.
.TP
.I /var/cache/transmission-navi/tmdb.json
Default TMDB metadata cache.
.TP
.I /usr/share/transmission/public_html/navi/
Static Navi interface served by Transmission. Its
.I catalog.json
entry links to the generated catalog under
.IR /var/lib/transmission-navi/ .
.SH SYSTEMD
.TP
.B transmission-navi-indexer.service
Runs one refresh.
.TP
.B transmission-navi-indexer.timer
Schedules periodic refreshes.
.SH SECURITY
The catalog contains media titles and SMB paths. Restrict Transmission to a
trusted network and enable its authentication when appropriate. Never place
Transmission or TMDB credentials in the static web directory or catalog.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR vlc (1)
.PP
Full installation and troubleshooting documentation is installed under
.IR /usr/share/doc/transmission-navi/ .
